---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  article
  title="About MutualLens"
  description="MutualLens is a preview project by Arhaan Aggarwal for readable follow-back comparisons with explicit source completeness and privacy boundaries."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE PROJECT</p><h1>Clarity over assumptions.</h1><p
    class="lede"
  >
    MutualLens is a project by Arhaan Aggarwal, built to make follower and
    following comparisons readable and explain what the data can actually
    support.
  </p>
  <h2>The intended product</h2><p>
    The primary requirement is website-only automatic checking for supported
    public accounts you own or manage. That integration remains blocked pending
    evidence of complete lists at the initial live target of approximately 6,000
    followers and 6,000 following, suitable access conditions, and a recurring
    zero-cash operating mode.
  </p>
  <h2>What this preview demonstrates</h2><p>
    The local comparison engine, synthetic sample, export importer, report
    interface, and optional browser snapshots can be explored independently.
    They do not establish that the automatic workflow works. Every preview
    document is marked noindex, and advertisements are disabled.
  </p>
  <h2>Readable by design</h2><p>
    The interface emphasizes lists, meaningful labels, and provenance. It avoids
    remote avatars, social embeds, and decorative profile lookups. Results
    describe supplied relationships without assigning motives or automating
    unfollows.
  </p>
  <p>
    Source code and development progress are available in the <a
      href="https://github.com/Arhaan2/mutuallens"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">MutualLens GitHub repository</a
    >. MutualLens is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by Instagram
    or Meta.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href={sitePath('/guides/')}>Browse the practical guides</a> or <a
      href={sitePath('/')}>return to the checker overview</a
    >.
  </p>
</Page>
